OnboardMimic Lab is bundled with OnboardMimic and shares its release version.
Source components retain their original licenses and attribution.

The Lab collection panel assets in src/onboardmimic_lab/static/ are adapted from
the OnboardMimic v0.1.2 development collection panel (Apache-2.0). The motion
console and controller assets are supplied by the containing OM installation.
The Apache-2.0 license text is included in third_party/openlambda/LICENSE.

Selected OpenLambda source files are retained under third_party/openlambda/,
with upstream LICENSE and NOTICE files. See upstreams.json for pinned commits.
Upstream names are preserved for provenance and are not a claim of authorship.

src/onboardmimic_lab/video_timing.py is copied from OpenLambda's
data_collection/robot/src/lambda_robot_data/timing.py (Apache-2.0).
The original license and notices remain in third_party/openlambda/.

src/onboardmimic_lab/lerobot_dataset.py adapts the Parquet/MP4 export design,
field naming, image crop/encoding settings and metadata layout from OpenLambda
data_collection/robot/src/lambda_robot_data/export.py (Apache-2.0).
OM changes: body-only profile, native consumed-token inputs, causal camera
alignment, verified publication/cleanup, and integrated replay compatibility.

lerobot_storage.py implements the documented LeRobot v2.1 layout and metadata
contracts, verified against Hugging Face LeRobot v0.3.3 (Apache-2.0), referencing
OpenLambda data_collection/human/src/storage/lerobot.py layout conventions.
